bleshooting cause) and release cadence in Ch 17 (where the three-supported-minors rule and the ~3/year cadence explain each other). Ch 7 (scheduling) and Ch 14 (Helm) are similarly thin and get named anchors.\n\n**Also specified:** four things that must *not* be retrieved — Ch 1 mechanics, the dated graduated-project roster (retrieve the maturity *levels* instead), the unpublished 60-question/75% figures, and any `[inferred]` trap framed as exam frequency.","numLines":19,"startLine":1,"totalLines":19}}}
